cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use PyOccult, please cite it as below. Parts of the code and documentation were
  developed with the help of Claude (Anthropic), an AI model, using Claude Code; all results
  were reviewed and validated by the author.
title: "PyOccult: asteroid occultation search for one observer site"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zahl
    given-names: Percy
    alias: pyzahl
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: "0.11.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pyzahl/PyOccult"
abstract: >-
  Portable Python replacement for the Occult occultation predictor: finds asteroid
  occultations of Gaia DR3 stars for an observer site (JPL Horizons orbits, NAIF SPICE,
  a local magnitude-limited Gaia catalog), with an all-asteroid target pick, shadow paths
  with 1- and 3-sigma limits, event previews and a local web interface. Validated against
  Occult Watcher Cloud.
keywords:
  - asteroid occultation
  - Gaia DR3
  - SPICE
  - IOTA
references:
  - type: data
    title: "PyOccult local Gaia DR3 catalog (G <= 16, G <= 18)"
    authors:
      - family-names: Zahl
        given-names: Percy
    identifiers:
      - type: doi
        value: 10.5281/zenodo.23113337
